        {"topic": "The ancient civilization that vanished overnight without a single trace", "hook": "An entire civilization vanished overnight with no explanation.", "script": "An entire civilization vanished overnight with no explanation. The Indus Valley Civilization was one of the most advanced of the ancient world. Running water. Grid-planned cities. A written language. Then around 1900 BC — nothing. No war evidence. No mass graves. No natural disaster. They simply ceased. Their language remains undeciphered. We still don't know why. Follow for history mysteries with no answers.", "keywords": ["ancient", "civilization", "mystery", "history", "indus"]},
        {"topic": "The ancient map that revealed a 500-year-old conspiracy", "hook": "An ancient map revealed a conspiracy hidden for 500 years.", "script": "An ancient map revealed a conspiracy hidden for 500 years. The Piri Reis map, drawn in 1513, accurately shows the coastline of Antarctica — a continent not officially discovered until 1820. How? Some believe it was copied from even older maps. Maps from civilizations we have no record of. The answer has never been found. Follow for history's most unsettling mysteries.", "keywords": ["map", "history", "conspiracy", "ancient", "mystery"]},
        {"topic": "The plague that wiped out half of Europe in just three years", "hook": "Half of Europe died in three years. Nobody knew why.", "script": "Half of Europe died in three years. Nobody knew why. The Black Death arrived in 1347 on merchant ships. Within three years, 25 million Europeans were dead. Bodies piled in streets. Doctors fled cities. People believed it was divine punishment. It wasn't until 1894 that scientists discovered the bacteria responsible. Five centuries of not knowing. Follow for history's most terrifying turning points.", "keywords": ["plague", "history", "medieval", "europe", "disease"]},
        {"topic": "The king so feared his name was erased from every record in history", "hook": "A king so feared, his own people erased him from history.", "script": "A king so feared, his own people erased him from history. Pharaoh Akhenaten abandoned Egypt's gods, created a new religion, and moved the capital. After his death, priests erased his name from every monument. Every statue. Every record. For 3000 years he didn't exist. Then archaeologists found him by accident in 1887. History buried alive. Follow for pharaohs history tried to forget.", "keywords": ["egypt", "pharaoh", "history", "ancient", "mystery"]},
        {"topic": "The year the sun went dark for 18 months and millions starved", "hook": "The sun went dark for 18 months. Millions starved.", "script": "The sun went dark for 18 months. Millions starved. In 536 AD a mysterious fog covered Europe, Asia and parts of Africa. Temperatures dropped. Crops failed. Snow fell in summer. Historians now call it the worst year in human history. A volcanic eruption likely caused it. Civilizations collapsed. Famine spread across continents. Follow for history's darkest forgotten years.", "keywords": ["history", "famine", "medieval", "disaster", "darkness"]},
        {"topic": "The invention stolen, patented, and used to make someone else a billionaire", "hook": "He invented it. Someone else patented it and got rich.", "script": "He invented it. Someone else patented it and got rich. Nikola Tesla invented alternating current, radio, and the foundations of wireless technology. Thomas Edison stole ideas. Marconi used Tesla's patents for radio and won the Nobel Prize. Tesla died broke in a hotel room. Edison became a legend. Today we know the truth. Follow for history's greatest injustices.", "keywords": ["tesla", "invention", "history", "science", "patent"]},
        {"topic": "The battle where 300 soldiers defeated an army of one million", "hook": "300 soldiers held off an army of one million.", "script": "300 soldiers held off an army of one million. At the Battle of Thermopylae in 480 BC, 300 Spartan warriors blocked a narrow mountain pass against the entire Persian army. For three days they held. Every Spartan died. But their sacrifice gave Greece time to regroup. Persia never conquered Greece. Three hundred men changed Western civilization. Follow for history's most heroic last stands.", "keywords": ["sparta", "battle", "history", "greece", "ancient"]},
        {"topic": "The secret tunnel under the Berlin Wall that freed 57 people in one night", "hook": "A secret tunnel under the Berlin Wall freed 57 people in one night.", "script": "A secret tunnel under the Berlin Wall freed 57 people in one night. In 1964, students dug a 145-metre tunnel from West Berlin into the East. It took months. The tunnel was barely wide enough to crawl through. On one night alone, 57 East Germans escaped to freedom. The tunnel was discovered the next day. 57 lives changed forever. Follow for history's greatest escape stories.", "keywords": ["berlin", "wall", "history", "escape", "cold war"]},
