        {"topic": "The man who woke up at his own funeral — and no one believed him", "hook": "He woke up at his own funeral. Nobody believed him.", "script": "He woke up at his own funeral. Nobody believed him. In 1995, a South African man named Sipho William Mdletshe was declared dead after a car accident. He was placed in a metal box for two days. He woke screaming. Workers heard him and released him. When he returned home, his fiancée refused to believe he was real. She thought he was a zombie. She left him. He survived death and lost everything. Follow for real cases stranger than fiction.", "keywords": ["horror", "death", "mystery", "real story", "survival"]},
        {"topic": "The voice recording found in an abandoned asylum that answered questions", "hook": "A voice recording in an abandoned asylum answered questions.", "script": "A voice recording in an abandoned asylum answered questions. Ghost hunters at the Waverly Hills Sanatorium in Kentucky captured audio of a voice responding directly to their questions in real time. Not pre-recorded. Not explainable by echoes. The voice knew their names. Names they had never said aloud inside the building. The recording was verified by three separate audio analysts. Follow for paranormal evidence that has never been debunked.", "keywords": ["asylum", "horror", "ghost", "paranormal", "recording"]},
        {"topic": "The twin who felt every injury her sister suffered from 3000 miles away", "hook": "She felt her twin's pain — from 3000 miles away.", "script": "She felt her twin's pain — from 3000 miles away. Identical twins Gemma and Leanne Houghton have documented cases of feeling each other's physical pain across continents. When Leanne fell into an epileptic seizure in a bathtub, Gemma — who had no prior warning — was suddenly overcome with a feeling she needed to find her sister immediately. She called. The bath was overflowing. She had seconds. Follow for twin phenomenon cases that science cannot fully explain.", "keywords": ["twins", "horror", "paranormal", "mystery", "science"]},
        {"topic": "The lighthouse keeper's last log entry — written after he officially died", "hook": "His final log was written after he officially died.", "script": "His final log was written after he officially died. The Eilean Mòr lighthouse in Scotland was found abandoned in 1900. Three keepers had vanished. The final log entry described a storm of unimaginable force — on a day when weather records showed perfectly calm seas. One entry read: 'God is over all.' The lighthouse clock had stopped. The meal on the table was untouched. No bodies. No explanation. Ever. Follow for real mysteries the world has never solved.", "keywords": ["lighthouse", "horror", "mystery", "ghost", "scotland"]},
        {"topic": "The forest where no animal has willingly entered in over 100 years", "hook": "No animal will enter this forest. Not for 100 years.", "script": "No animal will enter this forest. Not for 100 years. The Hoia-Baciu forest in Romania is known as the world's most haunted forest. Animals refuse to enter. Trees grow in perfect spirals for no botanical reason. Visitors report intense anxiety, nausea and temporary amnesia. Photographs taken inside show faces that weren't there when the photo was taken. Scientists have studied it for decades. No rational explanation exists. Follow for real locations that defy logic.", "keywords": ["forest", "horror", "haunted", "romania", "mystery"]},
        {"topic": "The painting that shows a completely different person every time you photograph it", "hook": "This painting shows a different face every time you photograph it.", "script": "This painting shows a different face every time you photograph it. The Crying Boy painting by Bruno Amadio became notorious in 1985 when The Sun reported that copies were found unburned in the ruins of house fires across Britain. The fires destroyed everything. The painting survived every time. Superstition spread. Fire stations refused to store the prints. The artist has never been conclusively identified. The faces in photos still shift. Follow for art mysteries that nobody can explain.", "keywords": ["painting", "horror", "mystery", "paranormal", "art"]},
        {"topic": "The apartment where 11 tenants vanished — all on the same day of the month", "hook": "11 tenants vanished from this apartment. Always the same day.", "script": "11 tenants vanished from this apartment. Always the same day. In the 1940s, the Leyendecker building in Germany recorded 11 missing persons cases across two decades. Each disappearance occurred on the 17th of the month. No bodies were recovered. Police investigations found no connection between the tenants. The building was eventually demolished. The land beneath it remains undeveloped. Local authorities have never offered an official explanation. Follow for real unsolved disappearance cases.", "keywords": ["apartment", "horror", "mystery", "disappearance", "paranormal"]},
        {"topic": "The child who described her previous death in exact forensic detail", "hook": "A 3-year-old described her own murder in exact detail.", "script": "A 3-year-old described her own murder in exact detail. A young girl from the Golan Heights told her parents she had been murdered in a previous life. She named her killer, the village, and the location of her buried body. Investigators found the village. Found the grave. Found the man she named — who confessed. The case is documented by Dr Ian Stevenson at the University of Virginia. Follow for reincarnation cases that even scientists couldn't dismiss.", "keywords": ["horror", "reincarnation", "mystery", "paranormal", "child"]},
        {"topic": "The clock that stopped at the precise moment its owner died — every generation", "hook": "This family's clock stops every time someone dies.", "script": "This family's clock stops every time someone dies. The Cornelius clock, an antique grandfather clock passed through a German family, stopped functioning at the exact moment of death of each successive owner — across five generations. Watchmakers found no mechanical reason for the stoppages. The clock would restart spontaneously days after each funeral. It sits in a museum in Bavaria. It has not stopped since the last owner died in 1987. Follow for objects that behave like they're alive.", "keywords": ["clock", "horror", "paranormal", "death", "mystery"]},
        {"topic": "The Victorian mirror found in a sealed room showing a room that doesn't exist", "hook": "This mirror shows a room that doesn't exist.", "script": "This mirror shows a room that doesn't exist. During a 1990s renovation of a Victorian home in Edinburgh, workers broke through a sealed wall and found a room untouched for over a century. Inside stood a large mirror. The reflection it showed was not the room it was in. Different furniture. Different wallpaper. A window where no window existed. Three workers refused to re-enter the room. The mirror was removed and destroyed. Follow for real architectural mysteries that refuse explanation.", "keywords": ["mirror", "horror", "victorian", "paranormal", "mystery"]},
        {"topic": "The surgeon who operated on himself and found something inside he couldn't explain", "hook": "He operated on himself — and found something unexplainable inside.", "script": "He operated on himself — and found something unexplainable inside. In 1921, Dr Evan O'Neill Kane performed an appendectomy on himself under local anaesthetic to prove the procedure was safe. Inside, he found an abnormality that no prior X-ray had detected — a tissue formation his colleagues called anatomically impossible. He survived the operation. He never publicly explained what he found. His private notes were sealed until 1989. Follow for real medical mysteries that science still can't categorise.", "keywords": ["surgery", "horror", "mystery", "medical", "doctor"]},
        {"topic": "The phone call received from a number disconnected 20 years earlier", "hook": "She got a call from a number disconnected 20 years ago.", "script": "She got a call from a number disconnected 20 years ago. Multiple documented cases exist of people receiving phone calls from numbers belonging to deceased relatives — numbers that telecom records confirm were disconnected years prior. In one case, the voice on the call described details of the caller's life that only the deceased could have known. Phone companies have investigated. No technical explanation has ever been given. Follow for real cases that make you afraid to answer the phone.", "keywords": ["phone", "horror", "paranormal", "ghost", "mystery"]},
